; A fixed TEXT arm keeps its spellable legacy variant name (`"x"` -> `X`), but the legacy
; keyword spelling `"self"` -> `Self` is not emitted raw. It falls back to the canonical UTF-8
; identity `Text73656C66`, shared by the type-choice and bare-member group-choice consumers.
; `c` shows explicit @name still selects exactly the authored public name; `d` is the spellable
; legacy control. These cover a fallback rather than a keyword-specific escape.
a = "self" / "x" / uint
b = [ true // "self" ]
c = "self" ; @name mine
  / uint
d = "type" / null / tstr
